    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-5212",
      "problem": "Consider the picture below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/f2518c2e998e7c7f551548a4cc7283720a66428ea8fa9872494a81cc3848ba9e.png)\n\nGiven that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/80eb0b356da6e6a2315ea1466d34b914c6cad5e59ff07c4d061ea82b69ed9838.svg), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/44db815dcaf0a9d405026460a655495e055df7e55a785f542f8920ca90af5418.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that when two known vectors are not parallel, a linear combination of them is unique. So, once we rewrite ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/a14e933631f2b075c5a0bb4ab14fad2ca2790c3be2122b1fe8f4b7193fb505b2.svg) in terms of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/c019067a8269a2742c3a6047869e770377f8cb10849abee7d66ccdf63db96ce0.svg) we can match coefficients to determine the unknown scalar.\n\nTo find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/4a2f3891f0b4c8b852767d556e1607028035219b70ab83b4910e95159a930b9c.svg) we want to match the expression\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/52599a11cea864ea801b87d8ec0ea288252afa4265395d9fbb4a4dc2815e9e7e.svg)\n\nWe are given that one of the components is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/a2b2f82b89941e4065ecf4c3bf612ab3d7e66fdb16c848dd2ce169480714e7ae.svg) So, we first draw the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/cbbad9d9d0e183ac112cfdf946b99fd00718e0c6856d1a75564925b0e2760e85.svg) from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/278f99df1e14fe0ebfb61bdb72262a62670dcaa60d322148bc3ee591b278ec2d.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/ea517ac4ca8e0bcf7ba48f23e66f100323d5485f1221219aacfbea9148f4a1af.png)\n\nNote that in ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/894c73e17be5470ca722125b5bce8359ff97e6b927293422ecf23a1c2c4cba83.svg), we have:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/ab1992cc2245d0821336430062e166b7a769f4240c3110cadd94159f0767650f.svg)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/1ae978d02b0e05cae043baed56dede840586c16b2270cd2bc01fa06f3e22b0d3.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) have the same direction\n\nHence, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/3e9ba7aac6024c4058689707c3ad521f885d6b0d3000131d826d7bb415d760dc.svg)\n\nAdditionally,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/c2f31143fbd86e027625006fdaa815453c0052be9f00645083d708b9e1a057ae.svg)\n\nConsequently, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/495720a4dfafe7999434529b57511fbc9f9d098a916b825a17405914c8c3c632.svg)\n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/e6090f180976846ce7a2e6e8d696a0fa078a471c950de6188908528c881839fb.svg) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/792ff38b4658d1d4bbfbc57cbe93be95dd8d90b24559f601250eaa81becf8d24.svg) we get:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251995/assets/b2cf4d169a51eeb0ee4258518496c5cc63abe8cf6a9e4c0e0a99dd1f5cae5728.svg)",
